Plast Reconstr Surg</source><year>1970</year><month>11</month><volume>46</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>514</fpage><lpage>515</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4919288</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Woolford</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Repair of nasal septal perforations using local mucosal flaps and a composite cartilage graft</article-title><source>J Laryngol Otol</source><year>2001</year><month>1</month><volume>115</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11233616</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kridel</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Considerations in the etiology, treatment, and repair of septal perforations</article-title><source>Facial Plast Surg Clin North Am</source><year>2004</year><month>11</month><volume>12</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>450</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15337112</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cottle</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nasal atrophy, atrophic rhinitis, ozena: medical and surgical treatment: repair of septal perforations</article-title><source>J Int Coll Surg</source><year>1958</year><month>4</month><volume>29</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>472</fpage><lpage>484</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13539430</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kridel</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Foda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lunde</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Septal perforation repair with acellular human dermal allograft</article-title><source>Arch Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg</source><year>1998</year><month>1</month><volume>124</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9440784</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yousef-Mian</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Repair of nasal septal perforation</article-title><source>Am J Rhinol</source><year>1997</year><season>Jan&#x02013;Feb</season><volume>11</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9065345</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>The hemitransfixion incision and the incision for mucosal advancement. The hemitransfixion incision was extended laterally to under the inferior turbinate for the lower mucosal flap and the other incision for the upper mucosal flap was made on the septal dorsum.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ceo-1-154-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>The nasal septal mucosa was not yet healed by the postoperative 5th week. ST: septum.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ceo-1-154-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>The nasal septal perforation was completely covered with nasal mucosal epithelium at the second postoperative month. ST: septum</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ceo-1-154-g003"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Presenting symptoms related with nasal septal perforation</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ceo-1-154-i001"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Etiology of the nasal septal perforations</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ceo-1-154-i002"/></table-wrap></floats-group></article>